
# 🚀 System Design — Nginx

## 1. 🏢 Monolithic Architecture

```text
        Client
          │
          ▼
   ┌──────────────┐
   │  Monolithic  │
   │ Application  │
   │              │
   │ Auth         │
   │ Users        │
   │ Orders       │
   └──────┬───────┘
          │
          ▼
      Database
```

**Monolith:** Everything runs as a single application.

---

## 2. 🧩 Microservices Architecture

```text
             Client
                │
                ▼
           ┌─────────┐
           │  Nginx  │
           └────┬────┘
                │
       ┌────────┼────────┐
       ▼        ▼        ▼
    Auth     User      Order
   Service   Service   Service
```

**Microservices:** Application is divided into independent services.

---

## 3. 🌐 Nginx Reverse Proxy

```text
Client
  │
  │ HTTP Request
  ▼
┌─────────────┐
│    Nginx    │
│Reverse Proxy│
└──────┬──────┘
       │
       ▼
 Backend Server
```

Nginx receives the client request and forwards it to the backend.

---

## 4. ⚖️ Nginx Load Balancer

```text
                  Client
                    │
                    ▼
              ┌──────────┐
              │  Nginx   │
              │   LB     │
              └────┬─────┘
                   │
        ┌──────────┼──────────┐
        ▼          ▼          ▼
    Backend 1  Backend 2  Backend 3
```

Nginx distributes traffic between multiple backend instances.

---

# 🛠️ Useful Nginx Commands

### Check Nginx version

```bash
nginx -v
```

### Test configuration

```bash
nginx -t
```

### Reload configuration

```bash
nginx -s reload
```

### Start Nginx

```bash
nginx
```

### Stop Nginx

```bash
nginx -s stop
```

### Check running process

```bash
ps aux | grep nginx
```

